Third-party components
----------------------

Coodra depends on and may bundle third-party open-source packages from the npm
ecosystem when building the published `@coodra/cli` package. Those components
remain licensed by their respective authors under their own licenses.

The published CLI leaves native runtime dependencies (`better-sqlite3` and
`sqlite-vec`) as npm-installed dependencies so the correct platform binaries
are installed on the user's machine.

Graphify
--------

Coodra can install and manage a local Graphify MCP runtime for code graph
queries. Graphify is an independent third-party open-source project and is not
owned by Matrix Maven.

Upstream project: https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify
Python package used by Coodra: `graphifyy[mcp]`

Coodra's documentation and CLI should describe this integration as
"Coodra-managed Graphify" or "managed Graphify MCP", meaning Coodra manages the
local wiring and artifact paths. It does not mean Matrix Maven owns Graphify.

Dependency license review
-------------------------

For each release, regenerate a dependency license inventory from the exact
published artifact and keep it with release evidence. The source repository's
root `LICENSE` only covers Coodra-authored code.
